S2 production-scale concurrent PostGIS load
Date: 2026-08-14 Asia/Tokyo
Environment: PostgreSQL 16.4 / PostGIS 3.4.3, arm64 Docker; client pgbench 14.23; TCP 127.0.0.1:55432
Command: ./run.sh S2LOAD

Dataset and profile:
- 100 tenants x 10,000 fields = 1,000,000 Polygon(4326) rows
- FORCE RLS; explicit tenant equality in every application query
- gist(tenant_id, geom) for KNN
- write-time bbox_min_x/max_x/min_y/max_y with tenant B-tree indexes for bbox prefilter
- 64 clients / 8 workers / offered 200 queries/s / 15 seconds per case
- bbox returns up to 1,000 rows: p95 <= 2,000ms (map initial display SLO)
- KNN returns 20 rows: p95 <= 500ms (general API DB/network budget)
- achieved >=95% offered rate; skipped=0; failed=0

