Conclusion:
- The original PostGIS-only bbox plan is rejected at production scale under FORCE RLS.
- Do not mark PostGIS operators LEAKPROOF and do not bypass RLS.
- Persist numeric bounding coordinates at write time, apply explicit tenant equality plus leakproof float comparisons first, then exact PostGIS &&.
- KNN keeps explicit tenant equality and the composite GiST.
- The spike passes. The bbox columns/indexes must be promoted into the production field migration before production-scale acceptance of the application API.
